%N A398638 Number of quasi-cubic graphs on 2*n + 1 vertices.
%C A398638 A quasi-cubic graph is a simple graph with one vertex of degree 4 and all other vertices of degree 3. By the handshake lemma, such a graph necessarily has odd order.
%H A398638 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Quasi-CubicGraph.html">Quasi-Cubic Graph</a>.
%e A398638 a(4) = 28 because there are 28 quasi-cubic graphs on 9 vertices.
